      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GOOD'N'YOU (1) looks the one to beat after two solid BM64 runs this campaign, firstly a close third at Newcastle and then a fifth at the Kenso when beaten just under three lengths after being well back on straightening. The return from metro mid-week company helps, and his wet-track Beaumont records add to the appeal. RIVER JORDAN (2) has winning confidence after beating Hidden News at Newcastle, with Reece Jones staying aboard. Not much depth to this race so expect him to keep the ball rolling. CLASSIC POCKET (3) has been below his best in two recent runs, but the first-time visor gives him a genuine reset point. Best ratings keep him in the winning mix. GEM TYCOON (4) brings a near-miss BM58 second from Goulburn recently. Tougher this time but a top four finish is within reach. THE WARRIOR (5) is racing well without winning. The addition of blinkers might add that extra spark required.",
